From fad9cb3d631c287314e2de2f190274fb8c866a01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Lambert <jacob.lambert@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:48:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Comgr] Update gfx12.5 XNACK ISA parsing expectations (#4992)

Upstream llvm/llvm-project#232080 restored XNACK on/off support for
gfx12.5, so `amdgpu12.50-amd-amdhsa--gfx1250:xnack+` now succeeds. The
stale `INVALID_ARGUMENT` expectation caused `parse-isa-name.c` to fail
on Linux and Windows.

Remove `REQUIRES: FixFromJacob` and check successful parsing and
ISA-name round trips for both XNACK signs on `gfx1250`,
`gfx1250-strict`, `gfx1251`, and `gfx12-5-generic`.

Validation: `parse-isa-name.c` and `isa-enumeration.c` both pass under
LIT with the current AMDGPU parser and regenerated target tables,
reusing existing LLVM/Comgr build objects. The original expectation
reproduces `FAILED: INVALID: SUCCESS`. No full LLVM rebuild was run.

LCOMPILER-2999

Upstream: https://github.com/ROCm/llvm-project/commit/fad9cb3d631c287314e2de2f190274fb8c866a01
Backport: Omit removal of the temporary FixFromJacob test requirement, which is absent in therock-10.1. All XNACK checks are retained.

---
diff --git a/amd/comgr/test-lit/parse-isa-name.c b/amd/comgr/test-lit/parse-isa-name.c
index 589af4ea89ea4..8a06f1e65bca3 100644
--- a/amd/comgr/test-lit/parse-isa-name.c
+++ b/amd/comgr/test-lit/parse-isa-name.c
@@ -68,6 +67,16 @@
 // RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu9-amd-amdhsa--gfx900:xnack+" SUCCESS
 // RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu9.4-amd-amdhsa--gfx9-4-generic:xnack+:sramecc+" SUCCESS
 
+// COM: Gfx12.5 targets support explicit xnack on/off settings.
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.50-amd-amdhsa--gfx1250:xnack+" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.50-amd-amdhsa--gfx1250:xnack-" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.50s-amd-amdhsa--gfx1250-strict:xnack+" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.50s-amd-amdhsa--gfx1250-strict:xnack-" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.51-amd-amdhsa--gfx1251:xnack+" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.51-amd-amdhsa--gfx1251:xnack-" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.5-amd-amdhsa--gfx12-5-generic:xnack+" SUCCESS
+// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.5-amd-amdhsa--gfx12-5-generic:xnack-" SUCCESS
+
 // COM: gfx900 supports xnack but not sramecc, so a sramecc feature is rejected
 // COM: regardless of the arch spelling; gfx801 supports neither sramecc nor a
 // COM: xnack+sramecc combo.
@@ -85,7 +94,6 @@
 // RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu10.30-amd-amdhsa--gfx1030:xnack+" INVALID_ARGUMENT
 // RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu11.00-amd-amdhsa--gfx1100:xnack+" INVALID_ARGUMENT
 // RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.00-amd-amdhsa--gfx1200:xnack-" INVALID_ARGUMENT
-// RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu12.50-amd-amdhsa--gfx1250:xnack+" INVALID_ARGUMENT
 
 // COM: The processor may be omitted; it is derived from the subarch.
 // RUN: parse-isa-name "amdgpu9.00-amd-amdhsa--" SUCCESS
